 possible to your team mates in 30 seconds without giving begins with or sounds like clues.\"}"}}]],["$","div",null,{"className":"page-header","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"container page-header-nav-wrap","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"page-header-content","children":[["$","h1",null,{"children":"Articulate Game Voiceover"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"page-header-sub","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"<p>Another tv advert for another great kids' toy</p>"}}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"page-header-arrows","children":[["$","$L3",null,{"href":"/micropolitics-suzys-beauty-salon","className":"page-header-arrow","title":"Micropolitics - Suzy's Beauty Salon","aria-label":"Previous: Micropolitics - Suzy's Beauty Salon","children":"‹"}],["$","$L3",null,{"href":"/what-is-explainer-video-voiceover","className":"page-header-arrow","title":"Explaining the Explainer Video Voice?","aria-label":"Next: Explaining the Explainer Video Voice?","children":"›"}]]}]]}]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"blog-post-body","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"container","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-post-main two-col","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-text-col","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$4"}}],false,["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-media-col","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"embed-wrap","children":["$","iframe",null,{"src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/qMfHdzdqBBo","title":"Articulate Game Voiceover","allow":"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture","allowFullScreen":true}]}]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-post-section two-col","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-media-col","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-post-img-card","children":[["$","img",null,{"src":"/assets/img/blog/articulate-game-voiceover.jpg","alt":"articulate-game-voiceover","className":"blog-post-img"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"blog-post-img-caption","children":"Articulate Game Voiceover"}]]}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-text-col","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"<h2>What is Articulate?</h2>\r\n<p>Articulate is the fast-talking description game for kids with between 4 and 20 players. Describe as many things on the cards as possible to your teammates in 30 seconds without giving \"begins with\" or \"sounds like\" clues. Sound easy? Well, that depends on who you're teamed-up with! Articulate is all about finding the quickest, easiest way to describe something to your teammates and it's so much fun.<br>\r\nArticulate for Kids follows on from the spectacularly successful adult description game and can now be played by kids as young as 6 and as old as 12. It's great when a game mechanic works so well that it translates perfectly to different audiences! Articulate is the perfect family game to play at Christmas and it was a lot of fun to work on the TV ad!</p>"}}]]}],[],["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-bottom-text","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"<h2>Looking for a voice with energy and fun?</h2>\r\n<p>As you can tell from my website, I love voicing these kinds of jobs. And as my daughter gets a little older, there's a really good chance she'll hear my work (I wonder if she'll recognise me?). My vocal tone is bright, happy, and quirky, which is seems to be a perfect match for toys and board game commercials! If you'd like a little help figuring out whether my voice is right for your project, please <a href=\"/contact-guy\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Get in touch!\">feel free to get in touch</a> </a>and ask me to provide a sample of your script.</p>"}}],["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-post-cta","children":["$","$L3",null,{"href":"/voiceover-news","className":"cta-btn cta-btn--outline","children":"← Back to News & Blog"}]}],["$","$L5",null,{"pageTitle":"Articulate Game Voiceover","pageUrl":"articulate-game-voiceover"}]]}]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"blog-related-strip","children":["$","div",null,{"c